edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186479511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479823 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fe0f5a4d-5c79-5a6e-821d-dd222e30da56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479830 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479830 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82477" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479830 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479830 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $B$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$, given that\n\n$\\,$ $T([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}2x \\\\ x-3y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479830 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "071d0b70-e887-5685-aa09-942aa6ae2d26" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479830 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nFirst, let's find the image of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -7\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 \\\\ -4 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479835 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479835 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38880" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479835 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479835 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[T(x)]_{B}$, given that\n$\\,$ $[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479835 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0f740568-e21f-5fbd-943a-06810f0bb27d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479835 #edb/ref 1074 "The image of $[x]_{B}$ relative to the basis $B$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{B} & =[T]_{B}[x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479845 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479845 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82452" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479845 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479845 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and let $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[T(x)]_{B},$ given that\n$\\,$ $[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479845 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3570dc7e-1a01-5006-842e-6d17aa9f3a4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479845 #edb/ref 1074 "The image of $[x]_{B}$ relative to the basis $B$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{B} & =[T]_{B}[x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479888 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186479773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479888 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38089" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479888 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479888 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[T(x)]_{B}$, given that\n$\\,$ $[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479888 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c2f444bc-6844-54b3-8db1-284a3e7b2b75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186479888 #edb/ref 1074 "The image of $[x]_{B}$ relative to the basis $B$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{B} & =[T]_{B}[x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-13 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
